# Nekostream Anime Download API

## Base URL
```
https://mapper.nekostream.site/api/mal/
```

## Endpoint
```
GET /api/mal/{mal_id}/{episode}/{timestamp}
```

## Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description | Example |
|-----------|------|-------------|---------|
| `mal_id` | integer | MyAnimeList ID of the anime | `61316` |
| `episode` | integer | Episode number | `1` |
| `timestamp` | integer | Unix timestamp (use current time) | `$(date +%s)` |

## Response Format

```json
{
  "Kiwi": {
    "sub": {
      "download": {
        "360p": "https://pahe.nekostream.site/XXXXX",
        "720p": "https://pahe.nekostream.site/XXXXX",
        "1080p": "https://pahe.nekostream.site/XXXXX"
      }
    },
    "dub": {
      "download": {
        "360p": "https://pahe.nekostream.site/XXXXX",
        "720p": "https://pahe.nekostream.site/XXXXX",
        "1080p": "https://pahe.nekostream.site/XXXXX"
      }
    }
  },
  "status": {
    "time": 1786627441,
    "cache_expires_in": "1 hours 30 minutes 31 seconds",
    "serves_from": "cache"
  }
}
```

### Server Keys
- `Kiwi` - animepahe (most common)
- `gogoanime` - Gogoanime
- `anivibe` - Anivibe

Each server contains `sub` (subtitled) and optionally `dub` (dubbed) objects with quality options: `360p`, `720p`, `1080p`

## Example Request

### cURL
```bash
curl "https://mapper.nekostream.site/api/mal/61316/1/$(date +%s)" --compressed
```

### Python
```python
import requests
import time

mal_id = 61316
episode = 1
timestamp = int(time.time())

url = f"https://mapper.nekostream.site/api/mal/{mal_id}/{episode}/{timestamp}"
response = requests.get(url)

data = response.json()
download_url = data["Kiwi"]["sub"]["download"]["1080p"]
print(download_url)
```

### Bash
```bash
#!/bin/bash
MAL_ID=61316
EPISODE=1
TIMESTAMP=$(date +%s)

URL=$(curl -s "https://mapper.nekostream.site/api/mal/${MAL_ID}/${EPISODE}/${TIMESTAMP}" \
    --compressed | jq -r '.Kiwi.sub.download."1080p"')

echo "Download URL: $URL"
```

## Notes
- Timestamp can be any recent Unix timestamp
- Response is compressed - use `--compressed` with curl or decompress in code
- Download links work directly with `curl -O -J -L "$URL"`
- Cache expires in ~1.5 hours